    "final_answer": "Based on the config file `config/lamp.toml`, the lamp has:\n- **range_nm = 18** (nanometers)\n\nThis wavelength of **18 nm** falls in the **extreme ultraviolet (EUV)** or **vacuum ultraviolet (VUV)** region of the electromagnetic spectrum.\n\n**Key characteristics:**\n- **Spectrum region**: Extreme UV (~10-124 nm) / Vacuum UV (~10-200 nm)\n- **Energy**: ~69 eV (using E = 1240/nm formula)\n- **Atmospheric absorption**: Strongly absorbed by air, requires vacuum operation\n- **Applications**: Semiconductor lithography, scientific research, specialized lighting\n\nThis is a very short wavelength that would require special materials and vacuum conditions to operate effectively."
